<note>
    <title>The Fork: A Brief History</title>
    <content>
<![CDATA[
<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM 'http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd'>
<en-note>
<h2>History of the fork</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Dining forks were used in Middle Eastern courts by the 7th century.</li>
  <li>Forks were common among the wealthy in Byzantium (10th-13th centuries).</li>
  <li>Forks reached Italy via a Byzantine connection in the 11th century and spread to France in 1533.</li>
  <li>Thomas Coryate brought fork use to England in 1608; adoption was slow among elites.</li>
</ul>
<p>Reference: <a href="https://research.calacademy.org/research/anthropology/utensil/forks.htm">California Academy of Sciences: Forks</a></p>
</en-note>
]]>
